> a blessed amulet of life saving (being worn)

Good, good.

> the blessed Eye of the Aethiopica
> the rustproof +0 Fire Brand
> the rustproof +0 Magicbane (weapon in hand)

Magicbane's a cool weapon, but to keep it cool requires you keep its
enchantment down, it has a small artifact damage bonus, plus it's an
athame.  I find that wizards can do well with a good backup weapon, for
those times when you're low on power -- the Amulet drains magic
whenever you cast while carrying it, and power never recharges fast
enough for me.

> a blessed fireproof +2 pair of speed boots (being worn)

Very good.

> a blessed greased rustproof +2 helm of brilliance (being worn)
> a blessed +2 silver dragon scale mail (being worn)
> a blessed rustproof +2 pair of gauntlets of power (being worn)
> an uncursed +0 cloak of magic resistance (being worn)

You have multiple sources of magic resistance.  Of course, it might be
considered a reasonable precaution to have a non-artifact (and thus
theft-target) source, myself I consider it overkill.  You may want to
consider replacing the magic resistance cloak with one of protection,
considering your low AC... but really, you should try to fix that by
enchanting all your +2 armor.

> an uncursed lizard corpse

Good.

> 6 cursed scrolls of teleportation

I like to use scrolls of teleportation as last-resort escapes, but
while you're carrying the Amulet level teleport will never work, so you
might want to get these uncursed.

> a blessed scroll of charging

I would go ahead and use this on the wand of wishing.  You don't have
to use the wishes right away, and the wand should be safe enough in the
bag.

> an uncursed ring of regeneration (on right hand)
> a blessed ring of levitation
> an uncursed ring of sustain ability (on left hand)

All rings outside of your bag are vulnerable to lightning attacks.  I
think reflection might guard against that, but even so I generally keep
my levitation source in the bag for safe keeping.

> a wand of wishing (0:0)
> a wand of death (0:4)
> a wand of magic missile (0:4)
> a blessed bag of holding

> a +0 pick-axe (alternate weapon; not wielded)

A pick-axe can be your best friend in Genhenom....

> an uncursed skeleton key
> 7 blessed wax candles

Get those candles in the bag!  The ceremony won't work if they get
cursed!  In case the bag gets cursed I like to keep out a bottle of
holy water, and in case the water gets cursed I like to keep extra holy
water in the bag.

> an uncursed magic whistle
> a blessed +0 unicorn horn

Keep the unicorn horn out.  It's also nice to have a potion of extra
healing or better on-hand for rapid sickness cure.

