Aaaah... you could wish for two blessed scrolls of genocide, which
would help you identify them and give you two genos, or you could try
to make one with a magic marker before hand -- as a wizard, you'd have
a non-insignificant chance of success, 1/3 I believe.

>   Also I have not been crowned inspite of a number of #offers
> (also I wasn't told the sequence to open the drawbridge and had to fly
> over to the other side).

There aren't many intrinsics you have left to pick up, and it looks
like you've already got the weapons you want for the ascent.
Meanwhile, prayer can be a potent source of emergency aid once you're
out of Genhennom with the Amulet (first ascensions tend to be fraught
with peril), and getting crowned wrecks your prayer timeout.


> I've got a scroll of charging so I could recharge the wand and get some
> wishes.  If I do that what should i wish for?

Do it, but save the wishes unless you know what you want.  A cloak of
displacement can be surprisingly useful but will lower your
cancellation, making you vulnerable to level-drain... but I've had two
ascensions wearing one without too much trouble.  Once you're of
sufficently high level, you'll probably never lose more than one level
to a vamp, and killing it will earn it back instantly.


> Now the horrors of Gehennom.  First, am I ready?  From the spoilers
> I've read, I don't think so.  Hp and Pw seem awfully low.  I also have
> a nagging feeling that I'm missing something.  What should i do at this
